{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-349991",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To find when the total amount is a minimum, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=0.$ First, we differentiate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1500+{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1500)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{0}^{t}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we solve $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=0$:\n\n$$\n3{t}^{2}-27=0\\,⇒\\,t=3\n$$\n\nSo there are two candidates for global extrema, $t=0$ and $t=3.$ To find out how much money is in the account when $t=3,$ we figure out $M(3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(3) & =1500+{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3{x}^{2}-27)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1500+[{x}^{3}-27x]{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =1500+[({3}^{3}-27(3))-(0)] \\\\  & =1500+[27-81] \\\\  & =1500-54 \\\\  & =1446\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1446<1500$, we conclude that the minimum amount is $$\\,1446$, and this will happen after $3$ days.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
